{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And Moses sent to call Dathan and Abiram.</b> Behold, Dathan and Abiram were the masters of this dispute along with Korah, as it says, \"Now Korah, Dathan, and Abiram took their stand before Moses, and men of the children of Israel\" (Numbers 16:2) — they were the ones who gathered the people against Moses and against Aaron. Now Moses had spoken to Korah and to all his assembly, and he further said to him, \"You and all your assembly\" (Numbers 16:11), for he spoke to him first because he was the greatest among them. Now those who gathered were also the assembly of Dathan and Abiram, and therefore he now wished to speak with them as well, and to warn them concerning themselves and all those who had gathered as their assembly, and to appease them with good words, words of consolation for Israel, for his words with Korah were an appeasement for the children of Levi alone. The sense of <b>And he sent</b> is that they had gone away from before him while he was speaking with Korah, and afterward, \"Moses said to Korah\" (Numbers 16:8) — he was still standing there before him, or because Korah the Levite was standing in the camp of Levi near the tent of Moses, for all of this was on the first day, as he said, \"You and they and Aaron, tomorrow\" (Numbers 16:16) — and that is the morning about which he said to them, \"In the morning YHWH will make known who is His\" (Numbers 16:5). And it is possible that Dathan and Abiram were prominent leaders of the assembly, more important than On son of Pelet, and if they had been appeased by him, On would have followed their counsel; therefore he did not send to him. Now he [On] did not come and was not with them and not with the assembly of Korah, for he departed from before him when Dathan and Abiram departed for themselves as Moses contended with Korah, and he did not remain there, for he had already reconsidered through the counsel of his wife who saved him, as our Sages say (Sanhedrin 109b). For behold, Scripture did not mention him among those swallowed up with Dathan and Abiram, and he was not within the assembly that gathered against YHWH among those who offered the incense, for they were two hundred and fifty besides the four mentioned at the beginning."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "Ramban quotes Numbers 16:2 in abbreviated form; the full verse reads 'וַיָּקֻמוּ לִפְנֵי מֹשֶׁה וַאֲנָשִׁים מִבְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל חֲמִשִּׁים וּמָאתָיִם.' The citation of Sanhedrin 109b follows standard printed editions; some witnesses read simply 'ק״ט' without the 'ב.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:06:09.331344093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}